// ORO dialog resources.
// The template is an EMPTY captioned dialog: every control is owner-drawn in
// OroDialog.cpp (WM_PAINT + mouse handling). Orbiter skins the caption bar
// itself (dark bar + red close button, cf. DLG_CAPTIONCLOSE), so the native
// frame already matches the dark theme.
#include "resource.h"
#include <windows.h>

// Size note: this DLU size is only a STARTING GUESS and is deliberately not the
// source of truth. DLU -> px depends on the shell font metrics, which vary per
// machine and DPI: 333 x 369 DLU is 500 x 600 px at the textbook (6,13) base
// units, but on the author's box the same numbers came out ~33% larger. So
// OroDialog.cpp forces the CLIENT area to DLG_W x DLG_H px in WM_INITDIALOG.
// Change the size THERE, not here.
// WS_THICKFRAME is what makes the panel VERTICALLY resizable (2026-08-16).
// Orbiter supports this: DialogWin::OpenWindow creates addon dialogs with a plain
// CreateDialogParam off this template and imposes no styles of its own, and the
// dialog manager branches on WS_SIZEBOX/WS_THICKFRAME in its own geometry code.
// Three stock plugins already ship resizable dialogs through the identical
// oapiOpenDialog path - ExtMFD, Framerate and LuaConsole.
// THE WIDTH IS LOCKED IN CODE, NOT HERE: WM_GETMINMAXINFO pins the horizontal
// track size, because the banner's height is derived from a 500 px width and the
// slider column was deliberately narrowed to 500 in 2026-07-30. Only the height
// is the user's, and its minimum is 500 px of client.
IDD_ORO_CONTROL DIALOGEX 0, 0, 333, 369
STYLE DS_SETFONT | WS_POPUP | WS_CAPTION | WS_SYSMENU | WS_THICKFRAME
CAPTION "ORO - effects control"
FONT 8, "MS Shell Dlg"
BEGIN
END

// THE HELP WINDOW. Same empty-template, owner-drawn approach as the panel above and the
// same dark palette, minus the banner. Resizable in BOTH axes, unlike the panel: nothing
// here is pinned to a width - the text word-wraps to whatever it is given - so there is
// no reason to take the axis away. Its size is remembered in Config\ORO\window.cfg beside
// the panel's height; it is deliberately NOT reopened on a new session.
IDD_ORO_HELP DIALOGEX 0, 0, 300, 320
STYLE DS_SETFONT | WS_POPUP | WS_CAPTION | WS_SYSMENU | WS_THICKFRAME
CAPTION "ORO Help"
FONT 8, "MS Shell Dlg"
BEGIN
END
